## 7. Vulnerability Taxonomy: "Content Security Policy (CSP) Gaps"

### 7.1 Description
CSP is an HTTP header that restricts which resources the browser is allowed to load. Without CSP, injected scripts (via XSS) execute freely. With a weak CSP (`script-src 'unsafe-inline'`), CSP provides no protection.

### 7.2 Common CSP Mistakes

| Mistake | Impact |
|---------|--------|
| **`'unsafe-inline'` in `script-src`** | Inline `<script>` tags (from XSS) execute normally |
| **`'unsafe-eval'` in `script-src`** | [eval()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/sw.ts#156-178), `new Function()`, and template literal injection work |
| **Wildcard `*.cdn.com`** | Attacker hosts payload on the same CDN |
| **Missing `frame-ancestors`** | Page can be framed by any origin (clickjacking) |
| **No `report-uri` / `report-to`** | CSP violations happen silently, you never know |

### 7.3 Detection
- **Header Check:** `curl -I https://trading.com | grep -i content-security-policy`
- **CSP Evaluator:** Google's `csp-evaluator.withgoogle.com`
- **Browser Console:** CSP violations show as red errors in Console.

### 7.4 Remediation
```
Content-Security-Policy:
  default-src 'self';
  script-src 'self' 'nonce-{random}';
  style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
  img-src 'self' data: https://cdn.trading.com;
  connect-src 'self' wss://ws.trading.com;
  frame-ancestors 'self';
  report-uri /csp-report;
```
Use **nonce-based** CSP for scripts (Vite supports this via `html-nonce` plugin).

