## 9. Vulnerability Taxonomy: "Cookie Security Misconfigurations"

### 9.1 Description
Session cookies are the keys to the kingdom. Misconfigured flags can expose them to interception, theft, or misuse.

### 9.2 Flag Matrix

| Flag | Missing Impact | Correct Value |
|------|---------------|---------------|
| [Secure](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/secureCache.ts#205-401) | Cookie sent over HTTP (interceptable) | [Secure](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/secureCache.ts#205-401) |
| `HttpOnly` | Cookie readable by JS (`document.cookie` — XSS steals it) | `HttpOnly` |
| `SameSite` | Cookie sent on cross-origin requests (CSRF) | `Strict` or `Lax` |
| [Path](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/sw.ts#61-67) | Cookie sent to all paths (unnecessary exposure) | `/api` or specific path |
| `Domain` | Cookie shared with subdomains (increases attack surface) | Omit (defaults to exact origin) |
| `Max-Age` / `Expires` | Session cookie (lost on tab close, but also no server-side timeout) | Set explicit expiry |

### 9.3 Detection
- **DevTools → Application → Cookies:** Inspect all cookies for flag presence.
- **Automated:** `Set-Cookie` header scanner in CI pipeline.

### 9.4 Remediation
```
Set-Cookie: session=abc123; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict; Path=/api; Max-Age=3600
```

